# Add project environment variables here when needed.

# URL of the companion Express server in server/ (run `npm start` inside server/).
# When set, the Sitemap Checker, Robots.txt Validator, and LLMs.txt Generator
# use it for server-side URL fetching instead of falling back to public CORS
# proxies. In production this should point at wherever server/ is deployed
# (see server/README.md) — must also be added to connect-src in index.html's
# CSP and to ALLOWED_ORIGINS when running the server.
# Local dev:  VITE_API_URL=http://localhost:3001
# Production: VITE_API_URL=https://free-seo-tools-server.onrender.com
#
# There is no CI build step — deploys are built locally and pushed to
# gh-pages by hand. Vite only reads VITE_API_URL from .env files at build
# time, so it must be set in a local .env.production (gitignored, not
# committed) before running `npm run build` / `npm run build:prerender`,
# or the deployed site silently loses server-side fetching and falls back
# to direct browser fetches that CSP/CORS will block for third-party
# domains.
